<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!-- Lite profile: tuned for low-RAM devices (2-3 GB), like an ONN streaming stick.
     The setup service copies this to the user profile and self-heals after updates.
     Takes effect after a Kodi restart (Kodi reads advancedsettings.xml at startup).

     Texture resolution caps (imageres, fanartres):
     Kodi caps decoded texture size, expressed as pixel height at a 16:9 area.
     Kodi 21 defaults are imageres 540 (a 960x540 budget for posters, thumbs and
     landscape art) and fanartres 1080 (fanart and hero backgrounds).
       imageres 405: about 44 percent less memory per poster than 540, and at TV
       viewing distance in a widget row it is visually near identical.
       fanartres 720: a safety cap only. Fanart and hero backgrounds are currently
       disabled in the skin settings, so this rarely bites.

     Redraws are limited to dirty regions to ease the weak GPU.

     Video cache: Kodi 21 Omega moved cache settings into the GUI and ignores
     <cache> blocks here. The setup service now sets them through JSON-RPC. -->
<advancedsettings>
    <imageres>405</imageres>
    <fanartres>720</fanartres>
    <gui>
        <algorithmdirtyregions>3</algorithmdirtyregions>
        <nofliptimeout>0</nofliptimeout>
    </gui>
</advancedsettings>
